but they just keep offering me money.

06:24.245 --> 06:27.915
<i>I do it, I get to go around the world.
I mean, did you see Sahara? Ha, ha.</i>

06:28.083 --> 06:31.754
That movie gave me an opportunity to
take an Airstream across the country...

06:31.919 --> 06:34.089
...and sell that picture
one person at a time.

06:34.256 --> 06:37.009
- You suck donkey ass.
- Hey, you can't prove that.

06:39.846 --> 06:41.431
That was so humiliating.

06:41.598 --> 06:44.601
Look at all the stuff I put myself through
just to get laid.

06:44.768 --> 06:47.396
Oh, don't worry.
One day, you'll find your soul mate.

06:47.563 --> 06:50.483
The sad thing is, I already did,
years ago.

06:50.649 --> 06:51.984
Tracy Flannigan.

06:52.151 --> 06:54.986
She was the greatest girl I ever met,
and I blew it.

06:55.153 --> 06:56.279
You should look her up.

06:56.446 --> 06:59.241
- Am I boring you?
- No, it's just... Long day.

06:59.408 --> 07:02.912
Well, I suppose I could look her up.
I wonder if she'd even wanna see me.

07:03.079 --> 07:05.415
I wasn't exactly the nicest guy
in the world.

07:05.582 --> 07:09.753
And then in high school,
I was violated sexually by my father.

07:09.920 --> 07:13.048
It happened on numerous occasions.
I was afraid to tell anyone...

07:13.215 --> 07:17.261
...because I felt like somehow
it was my fault.

07:17.428 --> 07:21.015
So you do go all the way.

07:26.771 --> 07:28.524
Well, here goes.

07:34.696 --> 07:38.409
Uh, Tracy? Tracy Flannigan?

07:38.576 --> 07:41.830
Oh, my God. Brian Griffin, is that you?

07:41.996 --> 07:44.499
Uh, yeah. It's me.

07:44.666 --> 07:48.002
And all he wants is to kiss you
just one more time.

07:48.169 --> 07:51.799
Wow, you sure look different
than the last time I saw you.

07:51.966 --> 07:53.342
Yeah. Haircut.

07:53.509 --> 07:56.595
So to get out of here,
I just make a left out of the driveway...

07:56.762 --> 07:59.224
...and drive as fast as I can?
- Wait, Brian.

07:59.391 --> 08:01.892
I'm actually glad you found me.

08:02.059 --> 08:04.771
There's someone I've wanted you
to meet for a long time.

08:04.938 --> 08:08.733
From the look of those toenails,
I bet it's that little Lamasil monster.

08:08.901 --> 08:10.903
Brian, this is Dylan.

08:11.070 --> 08:13.572
He's your son.

08:13.739 --> 08:14.990
Oh, no way.

08:15.156 --> 08:17.701
<i>Jerry, Jerry, Jerry.</i>

08:23.082 --> 08:26.043
Gosh, this is a lovely home, Tracy.

08:26.210 --> 08:30.340
That's so weird. It smells like
there's a cat, but I bet there's no cat.

08:30.507 --> 08:33.344
I've wanted you to meet Dylan
for a long time, Brian.

08:33.510 --> 08:36.305
Well, Brian, a son. How about that?

08:36.471 --> 08:39.934
<i>My God, this is more uncomfortable
than the goodbye in The Wizard of Oz.</i>

08:40.101 --> 08:43.271
- Goodbye, Tin Man.
- Goodbye, Dorothy.

08:43.438 --> 08:45.816
- Goodbye, Lion.
- Goodbye, Dorothy.

08:45.983 --> 08:48.861
And I think I'll miss you most of all,
Scarecrow.

08:49.028 --> 08:51.196
Oh, okay.
That's kind of an odd thing to say.

08:51.363 --> 08:53.616
Yeah, a weird comment
in front of all of us.

08:53.782 --> 08:56.035
